The Facebook-Cambridge Analytica scandal exposed data of 87 million users collected through a quiz app — convenience features that seem innocuous become attack vectors at scale.
Data breaches exposed 22 billion records in 2021 alone; every convenience feature that collects data creates a liability that persists indefinitely in corporate databases.
China's Social Credit System demonstrates the endpoint of convenience-surveillance integration: a unified scoring system that restricts travel, employment, and banking based on behaviour monitoring.
